    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Battlefield_Logistics\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 100)  # Set time limit to 100 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    depots = list(range(4))  # D0..D3\n    units = list(range(3))  # U0..U2\n    supplies = list(range(3))  # S0..S2\n    days = list(range(1))  # Day0..Day0\n\n    demands = [[[49.41], [48.14], [41.58]], [[40.14], [49.22], [27.3]], [[34.47], [23.7], [24.3]]]\n    depot_supplies = [[[40.37], [32.0], [33.5]], [[43.38], [27.44], [33.86]], [[38.02], [32.6], [34.72]], [[35.22], [36.66], [30.55]]]\n    transport_costs = [[2.26, 4.83, 1.72], [4.28, 2.46, 1.44], [3.13, 1.49, 4.15], [4.55, 4.31, 1.25]]\n    risk_costs = [[52.17, 106.95, 135.5], [85.76, 189.6, 140.15], [95.93, 93.69, 168.43], [113.74, 68.66, 80.8]]\n    supply_volumes = [1.77, 1.75, 1.91]\n    penalty_costs = [70.92, 88.15, 98.37]\n    vehicle_cost = 10.0\n    vehicle_capacity = 53.0\n    total_vehicles = 21\n\n    # Decision variables\n    # Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Amount of supply s from depot d to unit u on day t\n    flows = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                for s in supplies:\n                    flows[(d, u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Shortage of supply s at unit u on day t\n    slacks = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                slacks[(u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Number of vehicles on route d->u on day t\n    vehicles = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                vehicles[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Route d->u is active on day t (binary)\n    routes = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                routes[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total cost (transport + penalty + vehicle + risk)\n    obj = quicksum(\n        transport_costs[d][u] * flows[(d, u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        penalty_costs[s] * slacks[(u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        vehicle_cost * vehicles[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        risk_costs[d][u] * routes[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Depot capacity constraints: Total outflow <= supply\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for u in units) <= depot_supplies[d][s][t],\n                    name=f\"DepotCap_D{d}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Inflow + slack >= demand\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for d in depots) + slacks[(u, s, t)] >= demands[u][s][t],\n                    name=f\"Demand_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Vehicle capacity constraints: Total volume <= vehicles * capacity\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(supply_volumes[s] * flows[(d, u, s, t)] for s in supplies) <= vehicle_capacity * vehicles[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"VehCap_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Route activation constraints: vehicles <= total_vehicles * route\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    vehicles[(d, u, t)] <= total_vehicles * routes[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"RouteAct_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Fleet size constraints: Total vehicles <= total_vehicles\n    for t in days:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(vehicles[(d, u, t)] for d in depots for u in units) <= total_vehicles,\n            name=f\"FleetSize_Day{t}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Situation:\nThe brigade operates in a contested mountain-valley AO with limited ground mobility and intermittent air support. Four supply nodes\u2014Supply Depot Bravo (west corridor), Depot Charlie (central MSR), Depot Delta (northern ridge road), and Depot Echo (forward staging near FOB Alpha)\u2014must sustain the 3rd Infantry Battalion at FOB Alpha, the 1st Armored Company at Combat Outpost Sierra, and the Ranger Task Force at Patrol Base Kilo. Key routes include a valley MSR exposed to indirect fire and IEDs, a narrow mountain pass susceptible to rockfall and weather closures, a river crossing constrained by bridge classification, and an urban corridor requiring heavy escort. Enemy activity includes harassment fires and likely IED emplacement on predictable convoy patterns.\n\nMission:\nDeliver essential ammunition, fuel, and medical supplies to supported units during the current operational day while minimizing total operational cost, including transport costs, vehicle deployment costs, fixed route security risk overhead, and shortage penalties. Preserve combat readiness and control exposure by activating only the routes required to meet operational priorities.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Prioritize mission-critical demands; accept controlled shortfalls only where shortage penalties are lower than the combined transport, vehicle, and route activation costs.\n- Depot constraints: Outflows from each depot are bounded by on-hand stocks; do not exceed depot capacity.\n- Vehicle capacity: Loads per convoy are limited by vehicle carrying capacity and the volumetric weight of each supply type; allocate vehicles to routes accordingly.\n- Route activation: Convoys may move only on routes that are explicitly activated. Activating any depot-to-unit route incurs a fixed Risk Cost representing security overhead (escort teams, engineer route clearance, ISR tasking, communications), applied once per route for the operational day regardless of the number of vehicles dispatched on that route.\n- Fleet limits: Total vehicles employed across all routes must remain within the available fleet; balance route activation decisions against fleet size to avoid overextension.\n- Cost discipline: Favor lower-risk, lower-cost corridors and proximate depots to meet demands. Minimize the number of activated routes while preserving redundancy for critical items. Consolidate loads to reduce escort requirements without exceeding vehicle capacity or compromising route survivability.\n- Coordination: Engineer and EOD support aligned to activated routes; MP escort and movement control synchronized with maneuver operations; ISR coverage prioritized to high-risk segments; preplanned reroutes if denial or closure occurs.\n- Output: Activated route set, convoy allocations per route, and directed supply flows from depots to supported units for the operational day.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\nUnit Demands (Units x Supplies):\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1 | S 2\n-----------------------------\nU 0        |  49.41 |  48.14 |  41.58\nU 1        |  40.14 |  49.22 |  27.30\nU 2        |  34.47 |  23.70 |  24.30\nDepot Supplies (Depots x Supplies):\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1 | S 2\n------------------------------\nD 0        |  40.37 |  32.00 |  33.50\nD 1        |  43.38 |  27.44 |  33.86\nD 2        |  38.02 |  32.60 |  34.72\nD 3        |  35.22 |  36.66 |  30.55\nTransport Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2\n----------------------------\nD 0        |   2.26 |   4.83 |   1.72\nD 1        |   4.28 |   2.46 |   1.44\nD 2        |   3.13 |   1.49 |   4.15\nD 3        |   4.55 |   4.31 |   1.25\nRisk Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2\n----------------------------\nD 0        |  52.17 | 106.95 | 135.50\nD 1        |  85.76 | 189.60 | 140.15\nD 2        |  95.93 |  93.69 | 168.43\nD 3        | 113.74 |  68.66 |  80.80\nPenalty Costs per Unit Shortage: [Supply S0: 70.92, Supply S1: 88.15, Supply S2: 98.37]\nVolume per Supply Unit: [Supply S0: 1.77, Supply S1: 1.75, Supply S2: 1.91]\nFleet Parameters: Cost 10.0, Capacity 53.0, Total 21",
    "LLM_description_template": "Situation:\nThe brigade is executing sustained operations in a contested sector. 3rd Infantry Battalion is fixed along the eastern approaches and requires immediate resupply to maintain combat power. 1st Armored Company is preparing a relief-in-place and must top off fuel and ammunition to retain mobility and readiness. Reconnaissance Troop is operating forward of friendly lines and has limited access windows due to enemy observation. Ground lines of communication are intermittently interdicted by indirect fire, mines, and small UAS. Supply Depot Alpha, Supply Depot Bravo, Supply Depot Charlie, and Supply Depot Delta hold stocks of ammunition, fuel, and medical materiel. Terrain channels movement along a few predictable corridors; certain valley routes are exposed to long-range fires, while alternate tracks demand engineer clearance and dedicated escorts.\n\nMission:\nDeliver ammunition, fuel, and medical supplies from the depots to the forward units during the current operational cycle while minimizing total operational cost, which includes transport costs, deliberate shortage penalties, vehicle deployment costs, and fixed route security risk costs.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Depot capacity: Each depot\u2019s outbound shipments are limited by available stocks by supply type. Flows will not exceed on-hand quantities.\n- Unit demand and penalties: Each unit has defined requirements by supply type. Where necessary and risk-justified, controlled shortfalls may be accepted at a penalty cost; priority will be placed on mission-critical items to maintain combat effectiveness.\n- Vehicle capacity: Shipments are constrained by vehicle carrying capacity. Supply types have different volume factors, and total loaded volume per movement must remain within vehicle limits.\n- Route activation and risk: Activating a route from a depot to a unit incurs a fixed Risk Cost representing security overhead (escort teams, route clearance, electronic countermeasures, and overwatch). This fixed Risk Cost is charged once per route activated in the period, regardless of how many vehicles use that route. Additional per-vehicle operating costs still apply.\n- Transport costs: Movement along each depot-to-unit route accrues transport costs that reflect distance, terrain, and expected delays.\n- Fleet constraint: The total number of vehicles dispatched across all routes cannot exceed the available fleet. Vehicle allocations to individual routes must respect this fleet limit and the route activation status.\n- Approach: Prioritize resupply to engaged forces and life-saving medical support, consolidate loads to reduce the number of activated routes, and maximize loads per dispatched vehicle. Activate only those routes whose fixed security overhead and transport profile justify the operational gain. Accept limited, risk-informed shortfalls only when the associated penalty is lower than the combined transport, vehicle, and route risk costs. Maintain flexibility to re-task vehicles if routes are compromised.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\n{DEMANDS}\n{DEPOT_SUPPLIES}\n{TRANSPORT_COSTS}\n{RISK_COSTS}\n{PENALTY_COSTS}\n{SUPPLY_VOLUMES}\nFleet Parameters: Cost {VEHICLE_COST}, Capacity {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}, Total {TOTAL_VEHICLES}"
}